Just a follow up.  I have looked into it a bit and the comment.char argument that was in prior versions of sqldf was passed to RSQLite but RSQLite did not actually do anything with it -- RSQLite's import  functionality never had the capability to remove comments.  Thus the main change that has caused problems seems to be just that RSQLite no longer accepts arguments that it does not implement.  When using sqldf the way to remove comments is by using the filter= argument and it seems that this was always the case.  Should RSQLite implement a comment.char in the future then I hope to provide this in sqldf as well.

